r time  a simple wallet that snapped and stuck  right to your phone  the magsafe duo charger also some  third-party belkan accessories  and of course the magsafe puck charger  we'll also talk about which of these are  amazing  and which ones have been a bit  disappointing right  away vadim made an apple master plan  video about how apple had been planning  this for a while  and how magsafe will be so good that  people are going to want to upgrade for  this reason  and it will keep more people tied into  the ecosystem  so after nine months was vadim right  well right away our first experience was  with apple's case and maxi puck  before the iphone 12s arrived i bought  the clear case which is the only one  where you can actually see the magnets  and started running some tests which is  where i broke my first finding on  maxsafe  that was published all over the internet  first off the new iphone 12 cases cost  10  more than before so to buy a genuine  apple case you now have to spend at  least 49  so it definitely isn't cheap thankfully  we found that the magnetic connection  with the puck was decently strong  and the overall design seemed to be  really nice to perfectly align the  charger  but it's after that video where i  started testing  and found the first flaw in the system  and that was the charging rate  for standard qi devices on apple's mac  safe product page compatibility section  they listed the mac safe can not only  charge iphone 12s  but also iphone 11s 10s and even all the  way back to the iphone 8  as well as airpods and while this is  technically true  maxsafe doesn't seem to be a beefed up  qi charger because  in real world speeds with these older  devices as well as android phones  i found that they only delivered between  one to three watts of charging  instead of the 15 watt max safe rating  or even a 7.5 watt standard  slow wireless charging which we were  expecting that's pretty  slow in fact 7.5 watt wireless charging  is noticeably slower than  even the old 5 watt charging bricks that  took forever so  if you use a magsafe charger for your  iphone 11 pro max  it would take about 12 and a half hours  to charge  compared to two hours with a wired fast  charger  so it's no wonder that cases with max  safe alignment magnets  never caught on for the older iphones it  seemed like magsafe was brand new tech  that might be much more efficient  and my only conclusion was that apple  had to put a separate recoil  or section of the coil for regular qi  but as we move on  you'll see that we now know that that is  not really true  the promise of 15 watt wireless charging  was very  intriguing when apple finally added  wireless charging to their phones they  only allowed 5 watt wireless charging at  first  until it was bumped up to 7.5 watts  where android were  already using 10 and even 15 watt  wireless charging  i personally loved wireless charging and  have used it since they added it but  there's always been those issues with  proper alignment and speed  because it was so slow i only used  wireless charging by my bed for  overnight charging  but with that i was still having issues  waking up and my phone would be  completely dead  most of the time it would still show up  as charging but it wasn't perfectly  aligned  so the charge rate was so slow that it  was still draining  or it would shut off after max safe  alignment has been  amazing for this and my phone is  perfectly charged every morning  max safe alignment has been amazing for  this and my phone is perfectly charged  every morning  and with the puck if you want to lay in  bed and use the same charger you can  unlike most wireless pads as for the  second part  charging speeds i went in depth to see  just how much faster apple's 15 watt  maxi charging was  compared to standard 7.5 watt g charging  charging speeds were definitely faster  especially at lower speeds  but not hitting that double speed as it  would suggest based on the advertised  wattage  and overall it only charged 30 minutes  faster than slow wireless charging  and 15 minutes faster than a 5 watt  charging brick  that's mostly because of how fast apple  tapers down that 15 watts down to 12.5  and then down to just 6 watts pulled  from a 20 watt brick  but even with that the other features of  magsafe made it amazing for me  i am somebody who always wanted a  magnetic car mount which some cases  offered  but then you lost out on wireless  charging which i didn't want to do  plus i really prefer not having a case  making my phone thicker and covering  all of the premium materials maxsafe  allowed both of those to be used  at the same time we ended up buying a  ton of accessories to test and some of  them have been fantastic for me  and many aren't even true max safe and i  don't even mind  here's why one of the first was the  wallet it got a bunch of bad press at  launch but for me it finally allowed me  to keep a slim tidy wallet  because you couldn't overstuff it and i  finally got rid of that big wallet bulge  plus i could keep attached to my phone  if i ever was  just wanting to throw in a jacket or in  one pocket if i needed to carry  something else  i then got the moft wallet which isn't  as  nice or smooth on the back but it is  very flexible since it can hold  one more card and they are much easier  to get out  plus it can be used as a stand as well  the magnum strength was a little bit  weaker though  about that if you use a case it does  help a little bit  but not enough i didn't try the crazy  expensive  sleeve since that seemed like a  nightmare for those who use their phone  often  but the duo charger seemed like an  excellent idea just not a hundred thirty  dollars plus haven't had a twenty dollar  brick excellent  i bought a third party one for much  cheaper and even though the magnets are  weaker and you don't get the official 51  charging speed  i only use this for portable use so all  i have to bring with me is a usb type-c  charger that can handle my macbook and  then this mat to be able to charge my  apple watch and my iphone  this has been awesome just to keep in my  bag at all times because it's so small  and portable  and i typically only use it overnight so  saving 30 minutes of charging time is  negligible  oh and the official one doesn't even  offer full 15 watts  anyways with that for home use i  hesitantly dropped the money on belkin's  three-in-one charger  that is really well made and i don't  regret it one bit  it has been the most reliable and useful  wireless charger that i've ever bought  and it is so convenient to charge all of  my devices  but for those of you guys who are on a  budget we also tested the third party  one  that isn't as well made but it still  works great thanks to those max 8  alignment magnets  and once again the charging speed  difference don't really matter  and in the car i personally use two  chargers  a cheap third-party one that comes with  everything you need in my truck  and a puck holder in our tesla both work  great and hold the iphone without any  issues  and although i thought the much more  expensive official version would be much  better  it's not really and here's why when  apple showed off the insides of the coil  they made it sound very special and new  but in real world use efficiency doesn't  really seem to be that much better  my biggest issue with it is heat and my  phone dimming when i'm using my gps  or even other apps with wireless  charging using the magsafe connection  and even though apple cuts down wattage  very early with magsafe with backsafe  and their coil is supposed to be more  efficient  we don't really see it in the real world  both technologies put out a lot of heat  and the iphone doesn't really deal with  heat very well  because they don't have any cooling tech  built in like android phones  do and that brings us to the magnetic  battery banks  and you guys have probably seen that i  wasn't very happy with  apple's solution while waiting for this  we all expected max safe speeds that  could hit  15 watts even if it was brief but  instead we are limited to 5 watts  just like with regular qi and it's  actually slower than many third-party  options  with that there are also a ton of  limitations on when they will actually  even charge  what this shows us is that apple's  current coil and cooling tech  isn't much better than much older qi  solutions  and now we actually have proof chinese  qi battery packs have an efficiency of a  low  45 percent which is combined from the  losses of wireless charging  and pulling from batteries and apple's  solution is  55 because of this even though apple  makes great looking accessories  in terms of actual performance  third-party solutions can come  close to or even better than what apple  is offering  and with that to answer the question if  this will replace  lightning ports soon i think that apple  is still planning on that but it will  take a lot longer than they hoped  to me the biggest reason why is because  the battery pack was released  nine months after launch of the phones  where most companies would want to  launch it  right away to get the most sales when  people are buying brand new devices with  exciting new tech  they're excited about and then also  during the holidays since  other people can gift those packs to  people that just dropped the money  and can make use of that the way they  release them out of the blue and so much  later makes it seem  like they've been working on it for a  long time and they just couldn't get it  right  and had to settle on slow 5 watt  wireless charging  and just get the thing out there before  the next iphone's  launch most people expected it to be  able to be charged by magsafe either  with two coils or just from the one  but it can't and it obviously has attack  and it unlocks  reverse wireless charging but only on  the iphone 12  and it is insanely slow your main  charging  is from a lightning cable 